<item><title>Egypt sets private-sector minimum wage at EGP 8,500 from 2027</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/egypt-sets-private-sector-minimum-wage-at-egp-8-500-from-d6b3eb/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/egypt-sets-private-sector-minimum-wage-at-egp-8-500-from-d6b3eb/</guid><category>Egypt</category><description>The National Wages Council raised the floor from EGP 7,000, a rise of about 21.4 percent that takes effect on 1 January 2027.</description><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:25:31 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/egypt-sets-private-sector-minimum-wage-at-egp-8-500-from-d6b3eb/share.jpg" length="42688" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/egypt-sets-private-sector-minimum-wage-at-egp-8-500-from-d6b3eb/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
